# Sidelayout for Add/Edit Pages

All add and edit admin pages MUST open in sidelayout (`openSideLayout`) — not full-page navigation.

## Function

```javascript
openSideLayout(data, url, title, width = 75)
```

Helpers: `closeSideLayout()`, `generateSideLayoutEditLink()`, `generateSideLayoutAddButton()` in `assets/js/common.js`.

## Grid Add Button

```blade
<a href="javascript:void(0)"
   onclick="openSideLayout({}, '{{ getProjectUrl($grid_data['addurl']) }}', 'Add {{ $pageTitle }}'); return false;"
   class="btn btn-primary">
    <i class="fas fa-plus fa-fw"></i>
</a>
```

## Controller Edit Link (DataTable row)

```php
$editUrl = getProjectUrl('delay-registers/edit/' . Crypt::encrypt($id));
$row[] = '<a href="javascript:void(0)" onclick="openSideLayout({}, \'' . $editUrl . '\', \'Edit Delay\'); return false;" title="Edit"><i class="ri-edit-fill"></i></a>';
```

## Controller Form Action (sidelayout vs full page)

```php
if ($request->input('postKey') == 'sidelayoutContent') {
    return view('module.create-form', compact('pageTitle', 'data'));
}
return view('module.create', compact('pageTitle', 'data'));
```

Sidelayout loader sends `postKey: 'sidelayoutContent'` automatically via `openSideLayout`.

## Form Submission (CRITICAL)

- **DO NOT** use form `onsubmit` — use click handler on submit button
- **ALWAYS** use `ajaxRequestWithPromise`
- On success: `closeSideLayout()` + `reloadDataTable()` or `$('#ucList').DataTable().ajax.reload(null, false)`
- On error: keep sidelayout open, call `parseFormErrors(res, 'error')`
- Set title in `$(document).ready()`: `$('.sidelayoutTitle').html('{{ $pageTitle }}');`

## Select2 in Sidelayout

```javascript
$('.multiselect, .dd-select').select2({
    dropdownParent: $("#offcanvasRight")
});
```

